   "n": 40,
   "verdict": "revise",
   "name": null,
   "drop": [
    "Revelation 20:13"
   ],
   "note_fixes": [],
   "why": "Baptist/dispensational reader, and any reader of Revelation 20: the name is Acts 24:15's 'a resurrection of both the righteous and the wicked', but Rev 20:13 ('The sea gave up its dead ... each one was judged according to his deeds') says neither 'righteous' nor 'wicked' and does not say the two rise together. Placed under this name it makes Rev 20:13 the one general resurrection, which is the very question on the order of the last things (Rev 20:5-6) that the outline otherwise declines to settle by leaving 20:5-6 out. Dropping it leaves Dan 12:2, John 5:28-29 and Acts 24:15 (3 passages, within the bound); Rev 20:13's 'each one was judged according to his deeds' is already carried by Rev 20:12 under 'Found written in the book'."
